# [RATS](../wg/rats.html)

## Summary

The RATS Working Group held an interim meeting to discuss active drafts, security guidelines, platform-specific attestation profiles, and novel architectural extensions. The session covered security baseline guidelines for the RATS ecosystem, the Concise Reference Integrity Manifest (CoRIM) profile for Arm Confidential Compute Architecture (CCA), kernel and key attestation for Entity Attestation Tokens (EAT), a trajectory-based proof-of-humanity mechanism, and trustworthy acquisition of credentials. The group also evaluated the transition of the composite attester taxonomy from an active draft to an IETF wiki.

