## Decisions and Action Items

* **Decision:** The working group agreed to utilize the RATS Wiki for maintaining and evolving the taxonomy of composite attesters for the time being, with the option to publish it as an informational RFC once stabilized.
* **Action Item:** Tom Sato to write a detailed comparison between Kernel Identity and Attestation (KIA) and Linux Integrity Measurement Architecture (IMA) and share it on the RATS working group mailing list.
* **Action Item:** Muhammad Usama Sardar to submit a scoped revision of the security guidelines draft, focusing on a general security baseline and template guidance.